# Ask a promptable segmenter (kind: "segmenter", e.g. SAM 2.1 hiera-small)
# which pixels of the CURRENT wrist frame belong to the object in the jaws.
#
# Called by the HAL's vision attachment-evidence producer
# (openral_hal._vision_attachment_evidence.VisionAttachmentEvidenceProducer) at
# attach / detach / regrasp events — one shot per event, NOT per frame. The
# perception node (openral_perception_ros) captures the latest frame of the
# requested camera, projects the prompt point through that camera's manifest
# intrinsics, runs the segmenter, and returns its candidate binary masks. The
# producer then intersects each candidate with the same frame's depth channel,
# selects between them on geometry, and fits the bounded primitives of an
# AttachedCollisionObject.
#
# The prompt is GEOMETRIC, never semantic: unlike LocateInView (which takes a
# free-text query and returns labelled, scored boxes), this takes a 3-D point
# and returns "which pixels belong to the thing under it". The segmenter never
# classifies, and — see mask_scores_advisory below — the caller never gates on
# the model's confidence, nor picks between candidates by it.
#
# Request:
#   stamp            — attach instant being asked about. CALLER-owned, not
#                      server-stamped, so a trace replays against the frame
#                      captured at that instant (CLAUDE.md §1.8).
#   camera           — camera selector. Empty = perception node's
#                      primary/default camera; else one of its configured
#                      camera ids. NOT a hardcoded name.
#   frame_id         — tf2 frame tcp_point / negative_points are expressed in
#                      (e.g. gripper's attach link). Server transforms into
#                      the camera optical frame itself; TF2 stays the only
#                      source of coordinate frames (CLAUDE.md §2).
#   tcp_point        — positive prompt: Tool Center Point, 3-D, in frame_id.
#                      Sent as a POINT (not a pixel) so camera intrinsics stay
#                      on the perception side, out of the torch-free HAL.
#   negative_points  — optional negative prompts in the same frame (typically
#                      jaw tips), pushing the mask off gripper fingers. Bounded
#                      by manifest's segmenter.max_prompt_points.
#
# Response:
#   ok                    — true iff a frame was available and at least one
#                           mask cleared manifest's segmenter.min_mask_area_px.
#                           False → `masks` empty; caller MUST fall back
#                           conservatively (jaw-span box, evidence_kind
#                           GRIPPER_FORCE) rather than leave the payload
#                           invisible to collision checking.
#   camera                — camera id actually queried (echoes resolved
#                           default).
#   masks                 — candidate binary masks, sensor_msgs/Image mono8 at
#                           source resolution (255 = in mask, 0 elsewhere).
#                           PLURAL: with segmenter.multimask the model emits
#                           three NESTED hypotheses per prompt (subpart/part/
#                           whole); only geometry (jaw containment, extent,
#                           depth) can pick, so the segmenter (no depth) MUST
#                           NOT — it returns every candidate clearing
#                           min_mask_area_px, area-ascending, and the HAL
#                           producer picks against its own wrist depth frame.
#                           multimask false yields a one-element array.
#                           RAW mono8, not RLE: one-shot call, not a 30 Hz
#                           stream — a 640x480 mask is ~307 kB, at most three,
#                           inside the ~100 ms deferred-ack barrier the HAL
#                           already holds for depth. sensor_msgs/Image is
#                           already normative and introspectable with
#                           `ros2 topic echo`; RLE would need a bespoke
#                           encoder/decoder pair in the safety-adjacent path.
#   mask_scores_advisory  — model's own IoU/confidence per candidate, PARALLEL
#                           to `masks`. ADVISORY ONLY, recorded in the trace,
#                           MUST NOT be thresholded or used to pick between
#                           candidates: a mis-aimed prompt was measured
#                           returning a 59.8%-of-frame mask at this model's TOP
#                           score of 0.977. Every fail-closed gate on the
#                           caller's side is geometric, never this.
#   failure_reason        — typed string ('ROSPerceptionStale: …', empty on ok).

builtin_interfaces/Time stamp
string camera
string frame_id
geometry_msgs/Point tcp_point
geometry_msgs/Point[] negative_points
---
bool ok
string camera
sensor_msgs/Image[] masks
float32[] mask_scores_advisory
string failure_reason
